spans.s:
bhūtá, ppl.
 —1. become, been, i. e. past;
real;
 —2. having become, being, used in
composition w. its predicate as a grammatical
device to give the predicate an adj. form
w. number and gender [1273c], 6^7, 19^4, 29^4,
56^15;
 —3. as n. (that which has become,
i. e.) a being, divine (90^19) or human or
other; creature in general, 2118, 23, 57^18,
63^12; created thing, 58^19; world, 91^16;
 —4. as m. n. uncanny being, ghost, goblin,
 55^19;
 —5. as n. element; pañca
bhūtāni, five elements (earth, water, fire,
air, ether, of which the body is composed
and into which it is dissolved), 66^5, 68^9;
so 661, 3. [√bhū: cf. φῠ-τό-ν, ‘plant,
creature.’]
